# Branching: main only, with approval

`main` is production and the only base branch. There is no `develop`,
`release/*` or `hotfix/*` flow in this repo any more.

## Before any task (mandatory)

1. Run `git status` and `git branch --show-current`.
2. If there are uncommitted or untracked changes you did not make, **stop and
   tell the user**. Do not stash, reset, checkout over them, or delete them.
3. Do not write code on `main`.

## New branch — only with the user's approval

1. Propose a name and **wait for the user to approve it**:
   `feat/<short-name>`, `fix/<short-name>`, `chore/<short-name>`,
   `docs/<short-name>` (lowercase, kebab-case).
2. After approval, always branch from an up-to-date `main`:
   ```
   git switch main
   git pull --ff-only origin main
   git switch -c <approved-name>
   ```
3. Never branch from another feature branch or an old commit unless the
   user says so.

## Working on the branch

- One commit per item, clear message (`feat(...)`, `fix(...)`, `chore(...)`).
- Run `flutter analyze` and the related `flutter test` before saying it is done.
  New Firestore field → `firestore.rules` + `firebase/rules-tests/fixtures/write_keys.json`
  + contract tests in the same branch.
- Push the branch and open a PR to `main`. **The user merges.**

## Never without the user's explicit approval

- Commit, merge or push to `main`; force-push anything.
- `git reset --hard`, `git stash drop`, `git rebase`, deleting branches or tags.
- Deploy Firebase rules or functions, or anything to Odoo production.
  (Rules: by hand from `main` only. Functions: one by one, never a whole
  codebase, never `--force`.)
- Change the app version in `pubspec.yaml`.

## Never commit

Build outputs, logs or `.txt` reports, `xcuserdata` / Xcode user files,
`.venv`, `out/`, secrets or API keys.

## Also

- New behaviour ships behind a server flag, OFF by default.
- Reuse existing screens; no new UI without approval.
